{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1494433658,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwMDUzNzc4NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1512#issuecomment-300537784"},"message":"grr -- probably not calls to `gc` since when I shimmed all (hopefully) calls to git to call it with ` -c receive.autogc=0 -c gc.auto=0 `) -- the same story :-(  it sucks","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1494434592,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwMDU0MjI0Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1512#issuecomment-300542247"},"message":"ok -- the reason is Singletons !  what is happening is \n- created a dataset, thus initiated GitRepo for it etc\n- tarballed it, and removed original directory  (some batched processes remain running)\n- extracted tarball under the same path -- singletons kicked in\n- added a new commit\n- requested that stale GitRepo instance which is running within now non existing repo to give me information about the HEAD\n- kaboom!\n\nSo -- singletons should probably monitor also something about the original directory where they are running, e.g. inodes for their repo directory and verify that it is the same one whenever asked for already existing instance/path.","files":null},{"type":2,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1494434621,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE3OlJlbmFtZWRUaXRsZUV2ZW50MTA3Njc4OTExMg=="},"title":"Dataset.add fails miserably due to crash within GitPython -- if operated within \"reincarnated repo\"","was":"Dataset.add fails miserably due to crash within GitPython -- if operated within \"reincarnated repo\""},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1494492366,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwMDcyNDQ1NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1512#issuecomment-300724454"},"message":"Hm. Tried to reproduce the failure with test from within `test_gitrepo.py`\nDoesn't fail. So, there's something I missed in your description of the reproductional procedure, I guess.\n\n```python\n@with_tempfile(mkdir=True)\n@with_tempfile()\ndef test_GitRepo_flyweight_monitoring_inode(path, store):\n    # testing for issue #1512\n\n    repo = GitRepo(path, create=True)\n    with open(opj(path, \"testfile.txt\"), \"w\") as f:\n        f.write(\"whatever\")\n    repo.add(\"testfile.txt\", commit=True, msg=\"some load\")\n\n    # move everything to store\n    import os\n    import shutil\n    old_inode = os.stat(path).st_ino\n    shutil.copytree(path, store, symlinks=True)\n    # kill original\n    rmtree(path)\n    assert (not exists(path))\n    # recreate\n    shutil.copytree(store, path, symlinks=True)\n    new_inode = os.stat(path).st_ino\n    assert_not_equal(old_inode, new_inode)\n\n    # requesting HEAD info from old instance\n    hexsha = repo.repo.head.object.hexsha\n\n    with open(opj(path, \"testfile.txt\"), \"w\") as f:\n        f.write(\"whatever else\")\n    repo.add(\"testfile.txt\", commit=True, msg=\"new commit\")\n\n    # requesting HEAD info from old instance\n    hexsha = repo.repo.head.object.hexsha\n```\n\nMay be you can point me to the actual code pieces, that are producing this.\n\nEdit:\nSame for `AnnexRepo`. But:\nWhat exactly are the batched processes are you talking about? Triggered by what calls?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1494513513,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwMDgwOTc1OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1512#issuecomment-300809758"},"message":"Hey -- thanks for looking into it @bpoldrack !!!\nexact code is now merged:  https://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/master/benchmarks/benchmarks.py#L103  \n\nyou should be able to reproduce it by running those benchmarks, after removing adding a unique indexed suffix in line  https://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/master/benchmarks/benchmarks.py#L138   ... so let me try to reproduce:\n\n```shell\n$\u003e asv run --python=2.7 --dry-run --bench .*SuperdatasetsOperationsSuite.time_createadd -v HEAD^..HEAD \n.... lots of output -- make terminal wide ,....\n\n$\u003e git diff benchmarks/benchmarks.py\ndiff --git a/benchmarks/benchmarks.py b/benchmarks/benchmarks.py\nindex 31d0ffec..efeeef5c 100644\n--- a/benchmarks/benchmarks.py\n+++ b/benchmarks/benchmarks.py\n@@ -135,7 +135,7 @@ class SuperdatasetsOperationsSuite(SuprocBenchmarks):\n \n         # TODO -- remove this abomination after https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1512 is fixed\n         epath = opj(tempdir, 'testds1')\n-        epath_unique = epath + str(SuperdatasetsOperationsSuite.ds_count)\n+        epath_unique = epath # + str(SuperdatasetsOperationsSuite.ds_count)\n         os.rename(epath, epath_unique)\n         SuperdatasetsOperationsSuite.ds_count += 1\n         self.ds = Dataset(epath_unique)\n````","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1494513589,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwMDgxMDE0OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1512#issuecomment-300810148"},"message":"in your attempt you are dealing with GitRepo, not Dataset ... also try to request current branch hexsha I guess -- I believe it was that git batched command started by GitPython which was holding on ;)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1495015665,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwMjA0NjMzOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1512#issuecomment-302046338"},"message":"Update:\nI can reproduce it now, by adding an additional request of `repo.repo.head.object.hexsha` to the code above. So yes: This apparently causes GitPython to keep a git process running. And using `GitRepo` is sufficient for reproducing of course ;-)","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1497273203,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTExOTQzMzQ2OA=="},"status":2}]}